{{ja-see|あちら}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|か|なた|yomi=k,irr}}

Compound of {{compound|ja|彼|tr1=ka|pos1=distal pronoun: "that one yonder", far from both speaker and listener|な|tr2=na|pos2=old genitive / possessive marker|た|tr3=ta|pos3=ancient morpheme indicating direction}}.<ref name="KDJc">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten Concise}}</ref><ref name="DDJS">{{R:Digital-Daijisen}}</ref>  Compare the formation of {{m|ja|日向|tr=hinata||sunshine, a sunny place|lit=sun's direction, sun-facing}}, using the same genitive ''na'' and direction-marking ''ta''.

First attested in 883.<ref name="KDJc"/>

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|かなた|acc=1}}

====Pronoun====
{{ja-pos|pronoun|かなた}}

# {{defdate|from 1120}} the [[other]], the [[other side]]
#: {{ja-usex|'''彼方'''の[[神]]、クルフィックス|'''^かなた''' の ^かみ、^クルフィックス|Kruphix, God of '''Horizons'''}}
# {{defdate|from 1120}} that way; [[over there]], [[far away]], in the distance
# {{defdate|from 883}} he, she, it: general [[third-person]] pronoun, referring to a person or thing far from both speaker and listener
# {{defdate|from 883}} a time removed from the present, either in the past or in the future

